{"id":"word:hebrew:H6924","type":"word","title":"קֶדֶם","subtitle":"H6924 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"the front , of place (absolutely, the fore part , relatively the East ) or time ( antiquity ); often used adverbially ( before , anciently , eastward )","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קֶדֶם (H6924) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 87 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קֶדֶם (qedem) means the front , of place (absolutely, the fore part , relatively the East ) or time ( antiquity ); often used adverbially ( before , anciently , eastward ) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 5 10."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קֶדֶם","transliteration":"qedem","pronunciation":"keh'-dem","strong":"H6924","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6924","partOfSpeech":"n-m adv","forms":["קֶֽדֶם","קֶ֑דֶם","קֵ֖דְמָ/ה","קֶ֖דֶם","מִ/קֶּ֑דֶם"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",32],["HR/Ncmsa",24],["HNcmsa/Sd",22],["HD/Sd",2],["HC/Ncmsa/Sd",2],["HTd/Ncmsa",1],["HC/R/Ncmsa",1],["HNcmsc",1],["HR/Ncmpc",1],["HC/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"the front , of place (absolutely, the fore part , relatively the East ) or time ( antiquity ); often used adverbially ( before , anciently , eastward )","usage":"aforetime, ancient (time), before, east (end, part, side, -ward), eternal, × ever(-lasting), forward, old, past. Compare 6926 .","full":"H6924. qedem קֶ֫דֶם noun [masculine] front, east, aforetime ; — absolute ׳ק Deut 33:27 +, קֶ֑קֶם Judg 8:10 +; construct קֶדֶם Prov 8:22 ; once plural construct קַדְמֵי 8:23 ; &#8212; 1 location a. front , ׳מִקּ Isa 9:11 from the front (i.e. East), in front (opposed to מֵאָחוֺר ), וָק ׳אָחוֺר Psa 139:5 behind and before ; ׳ק אֶהֳלֹךְ Job 23:8 I go forward (opposed to אָחוֺר ) b. East: ׳הַרהַֿקּ Gen 10:30 (J) mount of the East ; ׳בְּנֵיקֿ = dwellers in the east, tribes east or northeast of Canaan 29:1 (E), Judg 6:3 , 33 ; 7:12 ; 8:10 ; 1Kin 5:10 ; Isa 11:14 ; Jer 49:28 ; Ezek 25:4 , 10 ; Job 1:3 ; ק ׳הַרְרֵי Num 23:7 , see Di Sachau: Reise (1883), 159 ff.165 ff. Dr in Hast. PETHOS ; ק ׳אֶרֶץ Gen 25:6 (J); מִקֶּדֶם מָֽלְאוּ Isa 2:6 they are full from the east (insert probably מִקְסָם קֶסֶם, , or &lt; קֹסְמִים before ׳מִקּ , compare Lo De Du Che Hpt Di-Kit); elsewhere ׳מִקּ = eastward: (I) in the east Gen 2:8 (2) on the eastern (side) 12:8 (J) Zech 14:4 ; ׳מִקּ לְ on the east of Gen 3:24 (J), 12:8 (J), Numbers 34: (P), Josh 7:2 (JE), Judg 8:11 ; Ezek 11:23 = Jonah 4:5 ; -3 eastward , with verb of motion Gen 11:2 ; 13:11 (both J). 2 temporal, ancient time, aforetime: a. ק ׳הַרְרֵי Deut 33:15 ancient mountains , compare ק ׳אֱלֹהֵי 33:27 , ׳מַלְכֵיקֿ Isa 19:11 , שְׁמֵיקֿ ׳בִּשְׁמֵי Psa 68:34 . b. ק ׳כִּימֵי Psa 44:2 in ancient days ; compare ק ׳מִימֵי from of old Isa 23:7 ; Micah 7:20 ; Lam 1:7 ; 2:17 ; Isa 37:26 = ק ׳לְמִימֵי ) 2Kin 19:25 (see מִן 9b (2)); ק ׳כִּימֵי Isa 51:9 ; Jer 46:26 ; ק ׳יַרְחֵי Job 29:2 months of old. c. ׳מִקּ from of old Micah 5:1 ; Isa 45:21 ; 46:10 ; Hab 1:12 ; Neh 12:46 ; Psa 77:12 ׳מִנִּיק 7; 8:2 springing out of, derived from, ancient times (compare Dr); מִקּ ׳יָמִים 77:6 ; 143:5 days from of old. d. ׳ק alone, as adverb anciently, of old Psa 74:2 ; 119:152 ; ׳כְּק Jer 30:20 ; Lam 5:21 ; ק ׳ישֵׁב Psa 55:20 he that sitteth (enthroned from) of old. e. beginning , מִקַּדְמֵיאָֿ֑רֶץ Prov 8:23 from the beginnings of the earth ; ׳ק מִפְעָלָיו 8:22 the beginning of his works (|| רֵאשִׁית ). [ קֵ֫דֶם ], with ה locative I. קֵ֫דְמָה adverb eastward, to, toward, the east ; — Gen 25:6 (J), Lev 1:16 ; 16:14 ; Num 34:3 , 11 , 15 ; Josh 19:12-13 , (all P), 1Kin 7:39 2Chr 4:10 ; 1Kin 17:3 = 2Kin 13:17 ; Ezek 8:16 (twice in verse); + north, south, west, Gen 13:14 ; 28:14 (both J), Num 2:3 ; 3:28 ; 10:5 (north, west, in ᵐ5 ), 34:10 (all P); also as noun after מְּאַת = eastern side , Exod 27:13 ; 38:13 (both P), + W Ezek 45:7 (strike out Co; read קֶדֶם Berthol Toy Krae), + north, south, wes